# Special route

A special route is a purpose-built page whose content and behaviour do not fit an ordinary publishing template. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/special-route/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

In this project, the relevant principle is a deliberately scoped custom component or documented native route. Use a special page only when a verified task cannot be served by the existing dashboard, setting or guide. Record its owner, route and compatibility boundary.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep the same headings, navigation, focus and status conventions as the rest of civica.uk. Specify the input data, allowed actions and empty/error states. Native navigation should continue to support browser history and ordinary links.

## Home Assistant boundary

A theme is not permission to take over arbitrary HA routes or private components. New pages must not invent backend services or expose private household data. The examples illustrate route information and a recovery state, not an installed custom panel.

